
(grammar [inflate [single]] for [inflate $])
(grammar [inflate [single] with [held]] for [inflate $ with $])

(instead of [inflate $obj])
    Inflate with what?
	(asking for object in [inflate $obj with []])

(refuse [inflate #magic-boat with #pump])
    Inflating it further would probably burst it.

%% IBOAT
#plastic-inflatable-boat
(* is #in #dam-base)
(name *)	plastic inflatable boat
(item *)
(flammable *)
(dict *)	pile valve
(* size is 20)
(appearance *)
	There is a folded pile of plastic here which has a small valve attached.
%% TODO: object action routine IBOAT-FUNCTION

(perform [inflate * with #pump])
    (* is $rel $room)
    (now) (* is nowhere)
    (now) (#magic-boat is $rel $room)
    The boat inflates and appears seaworthy.

(refuse [inflate * with #pump])
    ~(* has parent $room)
    ~(room $room)
    (The *) must be on the ground to be inflated.

(perform [inflate * with $])
    You would inflate it with that?
    (fail)


